# air-review environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env` and source it, or set the same names as repository variables /
# secrets in CI. Every value below is a placeholder shape, never a real value.
# Environment variables override air-review.yaml; see docs/configuration.md and
# docs/providers.md. `.env` and `.env.*` are git-ignored; only this template is tracked.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Provider (which API answers the review)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Preset id: openai | azure-openai | azure-foundry | bedrock | google | anthropic |
#            mistral | groq | openrouter | together | fireworks | openai-compatible
AIR_REVIEW_PROVIDER=openai
# Endpoint root, without the chat path. Overrides the preset's default URL.
AIR_REVIEW_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# The API key value itself (simplest for CI secret stores) ...
AIR_REVIEW_API_KEY=sk-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# ... or the NAME of another variable that holds the key (preset default shown).
AIR_REVIEW_API_KEY_ENV=OPENAI_API_KEY
# Short-lived access token (Microsoft Entra ID, OAuth gateways); sent as a bearer
# token and implies AIR_REVIEW_AUTH=bearer.
AIR_REVIEW_ACCESS_TOKEN=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOi...
# Auth scheme override for the endpoint (see endpoint.auth in docs/configuration.md).
AIR_REVIEW_AUTH=bearer
# Token-limit parameter name: max_tokens | max_completion_tokens (Azure defaults to the latter).
AIR_REVIEW_MAX_TOKENS_PARAMETER=max_completion_tokens
# Legacy alias for AIR_REVIEW_BASE_URL (still read; prefer AIR_REVIEW_BASE_URL).
# AIR_REVIEW_OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1

# Preset default key variables. Each preset reads its own variable when
# AIR_REVIEW_API_KEY / AIR_REVIEW_API_KEY_ENV are not set. Set only the one you use.
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx            # openai
AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx         # azure-openai
AZURE_AI_API_KEY=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx             # azure-foundry
AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK=ABSKxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx     # bedrock (API key, not SigV4)
GEMINI_API_KEY=AIzaxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx         # google
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx     # anthropic
MISTRAL_API_KEY=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx              # mistral
GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx             # groq
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx     # openrouter
TOGETHER_API_KEY=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx             # together
FIREWORKS_API_KEY=fw_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx         # fireworks

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model roles (one model or deployment name per agent role)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shortcut for the reviewer model.
AIR_REVIEW_MODEL=gpt-4.1
# Per-role models. The planner is deterministic today; its model slot is reserved.
AIR_REVIEW_MODEL_PLANNER=gpt-4o-mini
AIR_REVIEW_MODEL_REVIEWER=gpt-4.1
AIR_REVIEW_MODEL_VERIFIER=gpt-4o-mini

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Configuration file
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Path to the config file (otherwise air-review.{yaml,yml,json,toml} in the cwd).
# AIR_REVIEW_CONFIG=./air-review.yaml

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub (SCM adapter)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Token for reading the PR and publishing comments. The adapter reads, in order,
# the variable named by platform.github.tokenEnv, then GH_TOKEN, then GITHUB_TOKEN.
# In GitHub Actions `${{ github.token }}` is enough with pull-requests: write and issues: write.
GITHUB_TOKEN=github_pat_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# GH_TOKEN=ghp_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# Set automatically by GitHub Actions; read to detect the pull request (owner/repo, PR number).
# GITHUB_ACTIONS=true
# GITHUB_REPOSITORY=acme/storefront
# GITHUB_EVENT_NAME=pull_request
# GITHUB_EVENT_PATH=/home/runner/work/_temp/_github_workflow/event.json

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Azure DevOps (SCM adapter; see docs/azure-devops.md)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Token for reading the PR and posting threads. The adapter reads the variable named by
# platform.azureDevops.tokenEnv (default SYSTEM_ACCESSTOKEN), then AZURE_DEVOPS_ACCESS_TOKEN (Entra ID bearer),
# then AZURE_DEVOPS_EXT_PAT, then AZURE_DEVOPS_TOKEN. JWT-shaped tokens are sent as Bearer, PATs as Basic.
# Keyless from a signed-in Azure CLI:
#   export AZURE_DEVOPS_ACCESS_TOKEN="$(az account get-access-token --resource 499b84ac-1321-427f-aa17-267ca6975798 --query accessToken -o tsv)"
# In a pipeline, expose the job token to the step: `env: SYSTEM_ACCESSTOKEN: $(System.AccessToken)`.
# SYSTEM_ACCESSTOKEN=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOi...
# Personal access token for manual runs (scope: Code read & write).
# AZURE_DEVOPS_EXT_PAT=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# AZURE_DEVOPS_TOKEN=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# Predefined Azure Pipelines variables, set by the agent and read to auto-detect the
# adapter, organization, project, repository and pull request. Only set them by hand to
# simulate a pipeline locally (`--ci azure-devops --org --project --repo --pr` does the same).
# TF_BUILD=True
# SYSTEM_TEAMFOUNDATIONCOLLECTIONURI=https://dev.azure.com/acme/
# SYSTEM_TEAMPROJECT=Shop
# SYSTEM_PULLREQUEST_PULLREQUESTID=483
# BUILD_REPOSITORY_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
# BUILD_REPOSITORY_NAME=storefront
# BUILD_REPOSITORY_PROVIDER=TfsGit

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Output and colors
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1 = plain ASCII logs for CI (same as --plain).
# AIR_REVIEW_PLAIN=1
# 0 = no spinner or report reveal (same as --no-animation).
# AIR_REVIEW_ANIMATION=0
# Standard color switches (https://no-color.org). Any value for NO_COLOR disables color;
# FORCE_COLOR=0 disables, any other value forces color even without a TTY.
# NO_COLOR=1
# FORCE_COLOR=1
# TERM=dumb also disables colors and animation.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Telemetry (local only; nothing is ever uploaded)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pricing table as JSON, USD per 1M tokens, overrides telemetry.pricing in the config.
# AIR_REVIEW_PRICING={"gpt-4.1":{"input":2,"cachedInput":0.5,"output":8}}

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal / reserved
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local model runtime, only behind features.ollama (disabled in this build); used by scripts/e2e.mjs.
# OLLAMA_HOST=http://127.0.0.1:11434
# OLLAMA_API_KEY=xxxxxxxx
